00:10:11,240 --> 00:10:14,400
but about 10 people total.

234
00:10:14,400 --> 00:10:16,600
They're going to evolve based on those interpersonal

235
00:10:16,600 --> 00:10:18,600
relationships, so how they know each other,

236
00:10:18,600 --> 00:10:21,200
what they talk about, how they talk about,

237
00:10:21,200 --> 00:10:23,200
and their task behaviors.

238
00:10:23,240 --> 00:10:26,400
So we're going to be talking about not the tasks that you

239
00:10:26,400 --> 00:10:29,360
are doing in your teams, but the behaviors surrounding

240
00:10:29,360 --> 00:10:30,400
the tasks that you're doing it.

241
00:10:30,400 --> 00:10:35,240
So if you are working on a task, if you are doing some coding,

242
00:10:35,240 --> 00:10:36,560
how are you coding?

243
00:10:36,560 --> 00:10:38,200
Or who are you coding with?

244
00:10:38,200 --> 00:10:40,560
How are you talking to other people about what you're coding?

245
00:10:40,560 --> 00:10:42,640
And you can apply that to any other tasks

246
00:10:42,640 --> 00:10:44,960
that you're doing in your teams.

247
00:10:44,960 --> 00:10:47,000
There's a lot of different theories.

248
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:50,560
Actually, Wikipedia is a pretty good nutshell

249
00:10:50,560 --> 00:10:52,880
of what are all the different kinds of theories

250
00:10:52,880 --> 00:10:54,480
and how different kind of models we

251
00:10:54,480 --> 00:10:56,360
